+## Release 1.6.8
+
+Release 1.6.8 corrects a coverage defect found on 2026-11-05 while the coverage tables were rebuilt under the
+completeness rule of 1.6.7: a subcategory that a row's navigation links as a category page of its own (`/cp/...`)
+was skipped as "a category page or other page, not a product listing", so the listings only that page names were
+never read, and the row could still be called complete. The stored category pages of the nine CSV rows that have
+one (the 2026-11-04 census) link 106 such pages (Food: 49, among them "Chips", "Cookies", "Soda", "Water",
+"Juices", "Coffee" and "Tea"). The 1.6.6 coverage tables recorded 130 skipped links of this kind as out of scope:
+95 category pages and 35 shop, brand, search, product or account pages; for 56 of the 95 category pages no listing
+under the page's id is known. Each new test was first run on the frozen 1.6.7 collector (commit `7ee2fa1`, its
+tree extracted byte for byte, the 1.6.8 tests copied in) and failed there by its own assertion; it passes on
+1.6.8. A run now makes more requests: one per subcategory page (a navigation page, through the general API like
+every category page: 1 Scrape.do credit or 1 Oxylabs result) and the result pages of the listings those pages name.
+
+| Change | Until 1.6.7 | Where |
+|---|---|---|
